data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002: \\\"greet, tested\\\" — summary\\n\\n## What was done\\n\\n1. Created `src/greet.py`:\\n\\n```python\\ndef greet(name):\\n    return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"\\n```\\n\\n2. Created `tests/test_greet.py` using `unittest`, covering:\\n   - a normal name: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n   (Test file inserts `src/` onto `sys.path` so `unittest discover` run from\\n   the repo root, with `tests/` as the start directory, can import `greet`.)\\n\\n3. Ran the required command from the repo root:\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit status: 0.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\n- Branch: `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`\\n- Commit: `4cf0fb0` — \\\"Implement greet(name) with unit tests\\\"\\n- Files changed: `src/greet.py` (new), `tests/test_greet.py` (new)\\n\\nNo other files were touched; no extra features were added beyond what the\\ndispatch asked for.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

